--[[
=====================================================================
 Seed_Creatures.lua - every hostile and neutral creature in WoW Forever
=====================================================================
 Source: your four WoW Forever NPC lists (Alliance Hostile, Alliance Neutral,
 Horde Hostile, Horde Neutral). 6708 creatures. This file REPLACES the
 earlier Seed_A_*.lua, Seed_H_*.lua and Seed_Zephras_Isle.lua files.

 One row per creature:
   id      NPC ID                    name     its name in Forever
   zones   locations (see ZoneData.lua; a continent is listed only for creatures
           with no other location)
   ctype   creature type (Beast, Humanoid, Critter...)
   level   level or range from the list, for example "20" or "34 - 35" ("??" = unknown)
   class   its designation: "elite", "rare" or "boss". Left out for normal
           creatures. ("Rare Elite" is listed as "rare".) A level of "??" always
           means a boss, so every creature with level "??" is listed as "boss".
   A, H    how each faction is treated: "hostile" or "neutral". A faction that is
           left out does not have the creature in its log.

 The designation (class) comes from the list. In the Hunting Log you only mark
 a creature as a quest mob, or change its designation if the list is wrong (those
 changes can be reviewed with Show > Changed by you).

 Location notes: pieces that were not real locations ("Unknown", "Azeroth") were
 left out. A creature listed under both factions with different locations gets the
 locations of both.
=====================================================================
]]

